WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
 Compound butter, lemon
juice, parsley, garlic, boom.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.060
Really good.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.230
In this MasterClass,
you'll be able to gain

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.500
even more knowledge.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.200
But more important,
more confidence

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.940
in becoming the cook
that you want to be.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.650
We'll be working on
techniques and recipes focused

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.160
on the bounty from the sea.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.430
And we're gonna learn
how to do sous vide

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.440
cooking two different ways.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.572
And then one of my favorite
courses in any meal, desserts.

00:00:27.572 --> 00:00:32.140
Ah, right out of the oven,
just like grandma used to make.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.110
One of my first jobs
was as a poissonnier.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.350
And it was just an
extraordinary moment in my life.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.550
I got to work with so much fish.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.180
There's so much more variety
of fish than there is meat.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.960
We're going to cook our
branzino in salt crust.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.220
I want you to hear it.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.730
Dover sole-- it's a fish
that has a very firm flesh.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.710
And therefore, it's not
going to flake apart.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.170
It's a pretty easy fish to cook.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.480
To really get that
skin crispy, you

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.993
want to get all of that
water off of there.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:02.410
You notice all the
moisture that's

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.720
accumulating along my knife--

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:05.770
beautiful.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.730
This is something that I eat
maybe two or three days a week.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:13.146
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.340
Chocolate pots de crème--

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.350
it's a small dessert
but extremely rich.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.760
You could use a milk chocolate.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.320
You could even use a
dark milk chocolate.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.890
My spoon goes in
nice and gently.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.090
Look how smooth
and creamy that is.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.212
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.750
I want you to be enriched
in your cooking technique

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.790
and therefore, be able
to nourish yourself,

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.157
your friends, and your family.

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:39.740
And you may make a
couple of mistakes.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.760
And that's OK.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.640
I've made countless mistakes.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.950
But you just keep
moving forward.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.960
I'm Thomas Keller, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.310
[MUSIC PLAYING]

